        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "LuCl3·6H2O, H2L1, and dibenzoylmethane (DBM) were taken in 30 mL methanol/acetonitrile (1:1) and stirred at room temperature for 10 min to give a clear solution. Triethylamine was added dropwise, yielding a yellow solution that was stirred for 24 h at room temperature. The yellow precipitate was filtered and dried in air. X-ray quality crystals were grown from pyridine/toluene diffused by hexane at room temperature over two weeks.",
